WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.585
With Crowdin, engineers keep
strings in keyed files and sync

2
00:00:04.585 --> 00:00:06.151
them to translation projects.

3
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.322
Crowdin does this well,

4
00:00:08.322 --> 00:00:10.261
with context-aware AI,

5
00:00:10.261 --> 00:00:11.827
vendors, and review.

6
00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.052
General Translation keeps copy
in components and translates

7
00:00:16.052 --> 00:00:17.096
it in your build.

8
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:20.739
Write the copy inline
inside a T component,

9
00:00:20.739 --> 00:00:22.189
with no keys to manage.

10
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:28.107
Then npx gt translate writes
every language before each app

11
00:00:28.107 --> 00:00:28.675
build.

12
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.694
To keep your catalogs,

13
00:00:30.694 --> 00:00:35.117
npx gt upload first imports
your reviewed translations.

14
00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:38.528
Your team now ships
Portuguese with each release.
